.TH auto-change-group-gid 8

\" auto-man2man (used in generating subcommand lists) depends on this section
.SH NAME
.PP
auto-change-group-gid - Change numeric GID of a group

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-change-group-gid [--silent] groupname new-gid [directory ...]
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
--silent    Option to proceed without progress output
groupname   Name of the group whose GID is to change
new-gid     New numeric GID of the group
directory   Optional directories in which to update group ownership
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-change-group-gid
command changes the numeric GID (group ID) of group "groupname".
Users whose primary group is "groupname" are updated accordingly.

If --silent is specified, messages indicating the progress of
the change are suppressed.

If additional arguments are present following the groupname and
new GID, they are taken as directories and searched
for files and directories owned by "groupname", updating the
group ownership of all that match.

Note: No group ownerships are updated outside the directories
explicitly indicated.  This allows ownership correction, which
is time-consuming, to be done separately if desired.

Note: Although the underlying DragonFly|FreeBSD pw(8) command
accepts either group name or gid for GID changes, we currently accept
only name in order to simplify the Linux groupmod(8) interface.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-change-group-gid --silent joeuser 2001 /home/joeuser
.ad
.fi

.SH FILES
.nf
.na
/etc/group
.ad
.fi

